 "slug": "gta-physics/c07",
 "chapter": "Cliffhanger",
 "topic": "What if GTA6 physics were real?",
 "script": [
  {
   "beat": "p1",
   "text": "You open your eyes in the hospital bed again. The nurse doesn't look surprised this time. She looks scared."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p2",
   "text": "Because the room is dark. The whole hospital is dark. Out the window, the whole city is dark. And it's been a lot longer than four seconds."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p3",
   "text": "The backup generators kick in. The man in the suit is standing at the end of your bed. 'It didn't come back,' he says quietly. 'Not this time.'"
  },
  {
   "beat": "p4",
   "text": "Your phone buzzes. A video from Mom. Ellie, safe at home, holding a flashlight, waving at the camera. And over her head, very faint, there's a little green bar."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p5",
   "text": "So, is any of this real? The physics is. A ten-story fall really ends at fifty-four miles an hour. John Stapp really survived forty-six g. And a car at thirty really needs six car lengths to stop."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p6",
   "text": "Would you have made the dive? Tell me in the comments. And subscribe, because next time, we find out what happens when Ellie respawns."
  }
 ],
